---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.jsx';
import { chapters, tracks } from '../data/experience';

const email = 'hello@lloydgerry.com';
const linkedin = 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/lloyd-gerry';
---

<Base
  title="Lloyd Gerry"
  description="Lloyd Gerry — engineering manager and senior full-stack developer in Victoria, BC. Business school, a photography company, Amazon, and search and rescue."
>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  <header class="top">
    <a class="name" href="/">Lloyd Gerry</a>
    <nav aria-label="Sections">
      <a href="#story">Story</a>
      <a href="#path">Path</a>
      <a href="#now">Now</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero">
      <img class="portrait" src="/portrait.jpg" alt="Lloyd Gerry" width="200" height="200" />
      <p class="kicker">Victoria, BC</p>
      <h1>Hi, I’m Lloyd.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I studied business, sold electronics, ran my own photography company, worked my way from customer
        service to software at Amazon, and most recently led the engineering team behind
        a maritime intelligence platform. I also volunteer as a search-and-rescue coxswain.
        This is the long version.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="story" class="story" aria-labelledby="story-h">
      <h2 id="story-h" class="label">Story</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I’ve been technical since I was six — building computers and websites long
          before either was a job. But my working life started with people, not code.
        </p>
        <p>
          At 20 I started in technical support at West Corporation; six promotions later, by way of team
          lead, I was an
          operations supervisor with 120 direct reports and six managers.
          From 2007 to 2010 I sold consumer electronics at Future Shop and ran the
          floor as a manager on shift.
          I earned a business diploma in finance at Camosun College,
          which is still why I make the case for engineering work in cost and risk
          rather than elegance.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2009 I started LG Photography and ran it for seven years — commercial,
          product, and portrait work, plus everything else a one-person business needs:
          the portfolio, the website, and finding the clients. It’s still how I think about craft:
          get the light right and you need far less fixing afterwards.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2015 I joined AbeBooks, an Amazon company, in customer service. Over five
          years I moved into tier 2 support, trained new hires across offices, and became
          a technical account manager for Fillz — writing scripts for customers and
          running the daily priority meeting with the developers. I finished a web development
          diploma at Lighthouse Labs in 2019, and in 2020 crossed over to the engineering team in the same
          building.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since then: Perl and Java for the BC Ministry of Health, mentoring at Lighthouse
          Labs, an Ethereum data product at Ether Capital, leading LLM training-data work
          at Scale AI, and two and a half years at GSTS on OCIANA — first as the lead
          engineer, then as engineering manager for a team that grew from ten to sixteen
          without losing anyone.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since 2020 I’ve also volunteered with Royal Canadian Marine Search and Rescue
          out of Sooke, where I’m now a coxswain: the person in command of the boat and
          crew on a rescue. It turns out to be the purest leadership job I’ve had —
          clear goal, real stakes, and a crew that has to trust you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="path" aria-labelledby="path-h">
      <h2 id="path-h" class="label">Path</h2>
      <Timeline client:visible chapters={chapters} tracks={tracks} />
    </section>

    <section id="now" class="now" aria-labelledby="now-h">
      <h2 id="now-h" class="label">Now</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <p class="card-k"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Open to work</p>
          <h3>Senior developer or development manager</h3>
          <p>
            Full-time, in Victoria or remote. A team that ships to real customers, where
            I can either build on AWS or lead the people doing it.
          </p>
          <p><a href={`mailto:${email}`}>Get in touch →</a> · <a href="/Lloyd-Gerry-Resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="card-k">Also</p>
          <h3>Fractional engineering leadership</h3>
          <p>
            Part-time engineering management for teams of five to fifteen who need the
            role covered before they can justify it full time.
          </p>
          <p><a href="https://fractionalleader.co">fractionalleader.co →</a></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-h">
      <h2 id="contact-h" class="label">Contact</h2>
      <p class="big">Say hello.</p>
      <p><a class="mail" href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a></p>
      <p class="muted">
        <a href={linkedin} rel="me">LinkedIn ↗</a> · <a href="/Lloyd-Gerry-Resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a> · Pacific time
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="foot">
    <span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Lloyd Gerry</span>
    <a href={linkedin} rel="me">LinkedIn</a>
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>Email</a>
  </footer>
</Base>
